late.\",\"priority\":1,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[5]\"},{\"name\":\"Images\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Images referenced by each container in the template.\",\"priority\":1,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[6]\"},{\"name\":\"Selector\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Label selector for pods. Existing ReplicaSets whose pods are selected by this will be the ones affected by this deployment. It must match the pod template's labels.\",\"priority\":1,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[7]\"}],\"group\":\"apps\",\"kind\":\"Deployment\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"deployments\",\"verbs\":[\"create\",\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"batch.job\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/k8s/clusters/c-fwtnp/v1/harvester/batch.jobs\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/k8s/clusters/c-fwtnp/v1/harvester/schemas/batch.job\"},\"description\":\"Job represents the configuration of a single job.\",\"pluralName\":\"batch.jobs\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\",\"PATCH\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Status\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Status of the job.\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"},{\"name\":\"Completions\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"The number of pods which reached phase Succeeded. The value increases monotonically for a given spec. However, it may decrease in reaction to scale down of elastic indexed jobs.\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[2]\"},{\"name\":\"Duration\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Time required to complete the job.\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[3]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[4]\"},{\"name\":\"Containers\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Names of each container in the template.\",\"priority\":1,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[5]\"},{\"name\":\"Images\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Images referenced by each container in the template.\",\"priority\":1,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[6]\"},{\"name\":\"Selector\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"A label query over pods that should match the pod count. Normally, the system sets this field for you. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/labels/#label-selectors\",\"priority\":1,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[7]\"}],\"group\":\"batch\",\"kind\":\"Job\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"jobs\",\"verbs\":[\"create\",\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"kubevirt.io.virtualmachineinstance\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/k8s/clusters/c-fwtnp/v1/harvester/kubevirt.io.virtualmachineinstances\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/k8s/clusters/c-fwtnp/v1/harvester/schemas/kubevirt.io.virtualmachineinstance\"},\"description\":\"VirtualMachineInstance is *the* VirtualMachineInstance Definition. It represents a virtual machine in the runtime environment of kubernetes.\",\"pluralName\":\"kubevirt.io.virtualmachineinstances\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\",\"PATCH\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Age\",\"field\":\".metadata.creationTimestamp\",\"type\":\"date\"},{\"name\":\"Phase\",\"field\":\".status.phase\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"IP\",\"field\":\".status.interfaces[0].ipAddress\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"NodeName\",\"field\":\".status.nodeName\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"Ready\",\"field\":\".status.conditions[?(@.type=='Ready')].status\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"Live-Migratable\",\"field\":\".status.conditions[?(@.type=='LiveMigratable')].status\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"Paused\",\"field\":\".status.conditions[?(@.type=='Paused')].status\",\"type\":\"string\"}],\"crd\":true,\"group\":\"kubevirt.io\",\"kind\":\"VirtualMachineInstance\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"virtualmachineinstances\",\"verbs\":[\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"create\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"endpoints\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/k8s/clusters/c-fwtnp/v1/harvester/endpoints\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/k8s/clusters/c-fwtnp/v1/harvester/schemas/endpoints\"},\"description\":\"Endpoints is a collection of endpoints that implement the actual service. Example:\\n\\n\\t Name: \\\"mysvc\\\",\\n\\t Subsets: [\\n\\t   {\\n\\t     Addresses: [{\\\"ip\\\": \\\"198.51.100.9\\\"}, {\\\"ip\\\": \\\"198.51.100.10\\\"}],\\n\\t     Ports: [{\\\"name\\\": \\\"a\\\", \\\"port\\\": 8675}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"b\\\", \\\"port\\\": 309}]\\n\\t   },\\n\\t   {\\n\\t     Addresses: [{\\\"ip\\\": \\\"198.51.100.11\\\"}],\\n\\t     Ports: [{\\\"name\\\": \\\"a\\\", \\\"port\\\": 93}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"b\\\", \\\"port\\\": 76}]\\n\\t   },\\n\\t]\\n\\nEndpoints is a legacy API and does not contain information about all Service features. Use discoveryv1.EndpointSlice for complete information about Service endpoints.\\n\\nDeprecated: This API is deprecated in v1.33+. Use discoveryv1.EndpointSlice.\",\"pluralName\":\"endpoints\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\",\"PATCH\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Endpoints\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"The set of all endpoints is the union of all subsets. Addresses are placed into subsets according to the IPs they share. A single address with multiple ports, some of which are ready and some of which are not (because they come from different containers) will result in the address being displayed in different subsets for the different ports. No address will appear in both Addresses and NotReadyAddresses in the same subset. Sets of addresses and ports that comprise a service.\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[2]\"}],\"group\":\"\",\"kind\":\"Endpoints\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"endpoints\",\"verbs\":[\"create\",\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"rbac.authorization.k8s.io.rolebinding\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/k8s/clusters/c-fwtnp/v1/harvester/rbac.authorization.k8s.io.rolebindings\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/k8s/clusters/c-fwtnp/v1/harvester/schemas/rbac.authorization.k8s.io.rolebinding\"},\"description\":\"RoleBinding references a role, but does not contain it.  It can reference a Role in the same namespace or a ClusterRole in the global namespace. It adds who information via Subjects and namespace information by which namespace it exists in.  RoleBindings in a given namespace only have effect in that namespace.\",\"pluralName\":\"rbac.authorization.k8s.io.rolebindings\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\",\"PATCH\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Role\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"RoleRef can reference a Role in the cu