 configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"date\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"}],\"crd\":true,\"group\":\"instancetype.kubevirt.io\",\"kind\":\"VirtualMachineInstancetype\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"virtualmachineinstancetypes\",\"verbs\":[\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"create\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1beta1\"}},{\"id\":\"resourcequota\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/k8s/clusters/c-fwtnp/v1/harvester/resourcequotas\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/k8s/clusters/c-fwtnp/v1/harvester/schemas/resourcequota\"},\"description\":\"ResourceQuota sets aggregate quota restrictions enforced per namespace\",\"pluralName\":\"resourcequotas\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\",\"PATCH\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Request\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Request represents a minimum amount of cpu/memory that a container may consume.\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"},{\"name\":\"Limit\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Limits control the maximum amount of cpu/memory that a container may use independent of contention on the node.\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[2]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[3]\"}],\"group\":\"\",\"kind\":\"ResourceQuota\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"resourcequotas\",\"verbs\":[\"create\",\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"storage.k8s.io.csistoragecapacity\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/k8s/clusters/c-fwtnp/v1/harvester/storage.k8s.io.csistoragecapacities\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/k8s/clusters/c-fwtnp/v1/harvester/schemas/storage.k8s.io.csistoragecapacity\"},\"description\":\"CSIStorageCapacity stores the result of one CSI GetCapacity call. For a given StorageClass, this describes the available capacity in a particular topology segment.  This can be used when considering where to instantiate new PersistentVolumes.\\n\\nFor example this can express things like: - StorageClass \\\"standard\\\" has \\\"1234 GiB\\\" available in \\\"topology.kubernetes.io/zone=us-east1\\\" - StorageClass \\\"localssd\\\" has \\\"10 GiB\\\" available in \\\"kubernetes.io/hostname=knode-abc123\\\"\\n\\nThe following three cases all imply that no capacity is available for a certain combination: - no object exists with suitable topology and storage class name - such an object exists, but the capacity is unset - such an object exists, but the capacity is zero\\n\\nThe producer of these objects can decide which approach is more suitable.\\n\\nThey are consumed by the kube-scheduler when a CSI driver opts into capacity-aware scheduling with CSIDriverSpec.StorageCapacity. The scheduler compares the MaximumVolumeSize against the requested size of pending volumes to filter out unsuitable nodes. If MaximumVolumeSize is unset, it falls back to a comparison against the less precise Capacity. If that is also unset, the scheduler assumes that capacity is insufficient and tries some other node.\",\"pluralName\":\"storage.k8s.io.csistoragecapacities\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\",\"PATCH\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Created At\",\"type\":\"date\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"}],\"group\":\"storage.k8s.io\",\"kind\":\"CSIStorageCapacity\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"csistoragecapacities\",\"verbs\":[\"create\",\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"fleet.cattle.io.bundlenamespacemapping\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/k8s/clusters/c-fwtnp/v1/harvester/fleet.cattle.io.bundlenamespacemappings\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/k8s/clusters/c-fwtnp/v1/harvester/schemas/fleet.cattle.io.bundlenamespacemapping\"},\"description\":\"BundleNamespaceMapping maps bundles to clusters in other namespaces.\",\"pluralName\":\"fleet.cattle.io.bundlenamespacemappings\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\",\"PATCH\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"date\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-archi