tood by users, and perhaps by peripheral systems, for an identity * a principal that can be authenticated and authorized * a set of secrets\",\"pluralName\":\"serviceaccounts\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Secrets\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Secrets is a list of the secrets in the same namespace that pods running using this ServiceAccount are allowed to use. Pods are only limited to this list if this service account has a \\\"kubernetes.io/enforce-mountable-secrets\\\" annotation set to \\\"true\\\". The \\\"kubernetes.io/enforce-mountable-secrets\\\" annotation is deprecated since v1.32. Prefer separate namespaces to isolate access to mounted secrets. This field should not be used to find auto-generated service account token secrets for use outside of pods. Instead, tokens can be requested directly using the TokenRequest API, or service account token secrets can be manually created. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/configuration/secret\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[2]\"}],\"group\":\"\",\"kind\":\"ServiceAccount\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"serviceaccounts\",\"verbs\":[\"create\",\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"authorization.k8s.io.subjectaccessreview\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/authorization.k8s.io.subjectaccessreviews\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/authorization.k8s.io.subjectaccessreview\"},\"description\":\"SubjectAccessReview checks whether or not a user or group can perform an action.\",\"pluralName\":\"authorization.k8s.io.subjectaccessreviews\",\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"group\":\"authorization.k8s.io\",\"kind\":\"SubjectAccessReview\",\"namespaced\":false,\"resource\":\"subjectaccessreviews\",\"verbs\":[\"create\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"ext.cattle.io.selfuser\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/ext.cattle.io.selfusers\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/ext.cattle.io.selfuser\"},\"description\":\"SelfUser is used to retrieve the current user information.\",\"pluralName\":\"ext.cattle.io.selfusers\",\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"aggregated\":true,\"group\":\"ext.cattle.io\",\"kind\":\"SelfUser\",\"namespaced\":false,\"resource\":\"selfusers\",\"verbs\":[\"create\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"logging.banzaicloud.io.clusteroutput\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/logging.banzaicloud.io.clusteroutputs\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/logging.banzaicloud.io.clusteroutput\"},\"pluralName\":\"logging.banzaicloud.io.clusteroutputs\"