ce. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Pool Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Name of the pool to allocate an address from\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"},{\"name\":\"Pool Kind\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Kind of the pool to allocate an address from\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[2]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"date\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Time duration since creation of IPAddressClaim\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[3]\"}],\"crd\":true,\"crdJSONPathParsers\":{\"Age\":\"{.metadata.creationTimestamp}\",\"Name\":\"{.metadata.name}\",\"Pool Kind\":\"{.spec.poolRef.kind}\",\"Pool Name\":\"{.spec.poolRef.name}\"},\"group\":\"ipam.cluster.x-k8s.io\",\"kind\":\"IPAddressClaim\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"ipaddressclaims\",\"verbs\":[\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"create\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1beta2\"}},{\"id\":\"networking.k8s.io.ipaddress\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/networking.k8s.io.ipaddresses\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/networking.k8s.io.ipaddress\"},\"description\":\"IPAddress represents a single IP of a single IP Family. The object is designed to be used by APIs that operate on IP addresses. The object is used by the Service core API for allocation of IP addresses. An IP address can be represented in different formats, to guarantee the uniqueness of the IP, the name of the object is the IP address in canonical format, four decimal digits separated by dots suppressing leading zeros for IPv4 and the representation defined by RFC 5952 for IPv6. Valid: 198.51.100.7 or 2001:db8::1 or 2001:db8:aaaa:bbbb:cccc:dddd:eeee:1 Invalid: 198.51.100.8 or 2001:db8:0:0:0::1\",\"pluralName\":\"networking.k8s.io.ipaddresses\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"ParentRef\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"ParentRef references the resource that an IPAddress is attached to. An IPAddress must reference a parent object.\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"}],\"group\":\"networking.k8s.io\",\"kind\":\"IPAddress\",\"namespaced\":false,\"resource\":\"ipaddresses\",\"verbs\":[\"create\",\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"rke-machine.cattle.io.digitaloceanmachine\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/rke-machine.cattle.io.digitaloceanmachines\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/rke-machine.cattle.io.digitaloceanmachine\"},\"description\":\"DigitaloceanMachine is a Rancher CAPI infrastructure provider InfrastructureMachine.\",\"pluralName\":\"rke-machine.cattle.io.digitaloceanmachines\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"PUT\",\"PATCH\",\"GET\",\"DELETE\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"POST\",\"GET\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"str