ceClaim describes a request for access to resources in the cluster, for use by workloads. For example, if a workload needs an accelerator device with specific properties, this is how that request is expressed. The status stanza tracks whether this claim has been satisfied and what specific resources have been allocated.\\n\\nThis is an alpha type and requires enabling the DynamicResourceAllocation feature gate.\",\"pluralName\":\"resource.k8s.io.resourceclaims\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"PUT\",\"PATCH\",\"GET\",\"DELETE\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"State\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"A summary of the current state (allocated, pending, reserved, etc.).\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[2]\"}],\"group\":\"resource.k8s.io\",\"kind\":\"ResourceClaim\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"resourceclaims\",\"verbs\":[\"create\",\"dele