t be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"date\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"}],\"crd\":true,\"crdJSONPathParsers\":{\"Age\":\"{.metadata.creationTimestamp}\",\"Name\":\"{.metadata.name}\"},\"group\":\"hub.traefik.io\",\"kind\":\"APIPortal\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"apiportals\",\"verbs\":[\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"create\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1alpha1\"}},{\"id\":\"namespace\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/namespaces\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/namespace\"},\"description\":\"Namespace provides a scope for Names. Use of multiple namespaces is optional.\",\"pluralName\":\"namespaces\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"DELETE\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\",\"GET\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"POST\",\"GET\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Status\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"The status of the namespace\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[2]\"}],\"group\":\"\",\"kind\":\"Namespace\",\"namespaced\":false,\"resource\":\"namespaces\",\"verbs\":[\"create\",\"delete\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"fleet.cattle.io.clusterregistrationtoken\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/fleet.cattle.io.clusterregistrationtokens\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/fleet.cattle.io.clusterregistrationtoken\"},\"description\":\"ClusterRegistrationToken is used by agents to register a new cluster.\",\"pluralName\":\"fleet.cattle.io.clusterregistrationtokens\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Secret-Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Custom resource definition column (in JSONPath format): .status.secretName\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"}],\"crd\":true,\"crdJSONPathParsers\":{\"Name\":\"{.metadata.name}\",\"Secret-Name\":\"{.status.secretName}\"},\"group\":\"fleet.cattle.io\",\"kind\":\"ClusterRegistrationToken\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"clusterregistrationtokens\",\"verbs\":[\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"create\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1alpha1\"}},{\"id\":\"hub.traefik.io.apiportalauth\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/hub.traefik.io.apiportalauths\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/hub.traefik.io.apiportalauth\"},\"description\":\"APIPortalAuth defines the authentication configuration for an APIPortal.\",\"pluralName\":\"hub.traefik.io.apiportalauths\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"PUT\",\"PATCH\",\"GET\",\"DELETE\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"date\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"}],\"crd\":true,\"crdJSONPathParsers\":{\"Age\":\"{.metadata.creationTimestamp}\",\"Name\":\"{.metadata.name}\"},\"group\":\"hub.traefik.io\",\"kind\":\"APIPortalAuth\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"apiportalauths\",\"verbs\":[\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"create\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1alpha1\"}},{\"id\":\"apps.statefulset\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/apps.statefulsets\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/apps.statefulset\"},\"description\":\"StatefulSet represents a set of pods with consistent identities. Identities are defined as:\\n  - Network: A single stable DNS and hostname.\\n  - Storage: As many VolumeClaims as requested.\\n\\nThe StatefulSet guarantees that a given network identity will always map to the same storage identity.\",\"pluralName\":\"apps.statefulsets\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Ready\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Number of the pod with ready state\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[2]\"},{\"name\":\"Containers\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Names of each container in the template.\",\"priority\":1,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[3]\"},{\"name\":\"Images\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"Images referenced by each container in the template.\",\"priority\":1,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[4]\"}],\"group\":\"apps\",\"kind\":\"StatefulSet\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"statefulsets\",\"verbs\":[\"create\",\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"userpreference\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/userpreferences\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/userpreference\"},\"pluralName\":\"userpreferences\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"GET\",\"PUT\",\"DELETE\"],\"resourceFields\":{\"data\":{\"type\":\"map[string]\",\"create\":true,\"update\":true}},\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\"]},{\"id\":\"storage.k8s.io.csistoragecapacity\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/storage.k8s.io.csistoragecapacities\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/storage.k8s.io.csistoragecapacity\"},\"description\":\"CSIStorageCapacity stores the result of one CSI GetCapacity call. For a given StorageClass, this describes the available capacity in a particular topology segment.  This can be used when considering where to instantiate new PersistentVolumes.\\n\\nFor example this can express things like: - StorageClass \\\"standard\\\" has \\\"1234 GiB\\\" available in \\\"topology.kubernetes.io/zone=us-east1\\\" - StorageClass \\\"localssd\\\" has \\\"10 GiB\\\" available in \\\"kubernetes.io/hostname=knode-abc123\\\"\\n\\nThe following three cases all imply that no capacity is available for a certain combination: - no object exists with suitable topology and storage class name - such an object exists, but the capacity is unset - such an object exists, but the capacity is zero\\n\\nThe producer of these objects can decide which approach is more suitable.\\n\\nThey are consumed by the kube-scheduler when a CSI driver opts into capacity-aware scheduling with CSIDriverSpec.StorageCapacity. The scheduler compares the MaximumVolumeSize against the requested size of pending volumes to filter out unsuitable nodes. If MaximumVolumeSize is unset, it falls back to a comparison against the less precise Capacity. If that is also unset, the scheduler assumes that capacity is insufficient and tries some other node.\",\"pluralName\":\"storage.k8s.io.csistoragecapacities\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Created At\",\"type\":\"date\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"}],\"group\":\"storage.k8s.io\",\"kind\":\"CSIStorageCapacity\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"csistoragecapacities\",\"verbs\":[\"create\",\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"discovery.k8s.io.endpointslice\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/discovery.k8s.io.endpointslices\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/discovery.k8s.io.endpointslice\"},\"description\":\"EndpointSlice represents a set of service endpoints. Most EndpointSlices are created by the EndpointSlice controller to represent the Pods selected by Service objects. For a given service there may be multiple EndpointSlice objects which must be joined to produce the full set of endpoints; you can find all of the slices for a given service by listing EndpointSlices in the service's namespace whose `kubernetes.io/service-name` label contains the service's name.\",\"pluralName\":\"discovery.k8s.io.endpointslices\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"PATCH\",\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"AddressType\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"addressType specifies the type of address carried by this EndpointSlice. All addresses in this slice must be the same type. This field is immutable after creation. The following address types are currently supported: * IPv4: Represents an IPv4 Address. * IPv6: Represents an IPv6 Address. * FQDN: Represents a Fully Qualified Domain Name.\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"},{\"name\":\"Ports\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"ports specifies the list of network ports exposed by each endpoint in this slice. Each port must have a unique name. When ports is empty, it indicates that there are no defined ports. When a port is defined with a nil port value, it indicates \\\"all ports\\\". Each slice may include a maximum of 100 ports.\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[2]\"},{\"name\":\"Endpoints\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"endpoints is a list of unique endpoints in this slice. Each slice may include a maximum of 1000 endpoints.\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[3]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[4]\"}],\"group\":\"discovery.k8s.io\",\"kind\":\"EndpointSlice\",\"namespaced\":true,\"resource\":\"endpointslices\",\"verbs\":[\"create\",\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"fleet.cattle.io.content\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/fleet.cattle.io.contents\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/fleet.cattle.io.content\"},\"description\":\"Content is used internally by Fleet and should not be used directly. It\\ncontains the resources from a bundle for a specific target cluster.\",\"pluralName\":\"fleet.cattle.io.contents\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"date\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"}],\"crd\":true,\"crdJSONPathParsers\":{\"Age\":\"{.metadata.creationTimestamp}\",\"Name\":\"{.metadata.name}\"},\"group\":\"fleet.cattle.io\",\"kind\":\"Content\",\"namespaced\":false,\"resource\":\"contents\",\"verbs\":[\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"create\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1alpha1\"}},{\"id\":\"node.k8s.io.runtimeclass\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/node.k8s.io.runtimeclasses\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/node.k8s.io.runtimeclass\"},\"description\":\"RuntimeClass defines a class of container runtime supported in the cluster. The RuntimeClass is used to determine which container runtime is used to run all containers in a pod. RuntimeClasses are manually defined by a user or cluster provisioner, and referenced in the PodSpec. The Kubelet is responsible for resolving the RuntimeClassName reference before running the pod.  For more details, see https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/containers/runtime-class/\",\"pluralName\":\"node.k8s.io.runtimeclasses\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"PATCH\",\"GET\",\"DELETE\",\"PUT\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"POST\",\"GET\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Handler\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[2]\"}],\"group\":\"node.k8s.io\",\"kind\":\"RuntimeClass\",\"namespaced\":false,\"resource\":\"runtimeclasses\",\"verbs\":[\"create\",\"delete\",\"deletecollection\",\"get\",\"list\",\"patch\",\"update\",\"watch\"],\"version\":\"v1\"}},{\"id\":\"management.cattle.io.projectroletemplatebinding\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"links\":{\"collection\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/management.cattle.io.projectroletemplatebindings\",\"self\":\"https://harvester.invalid/v1/schemas/management.cattle.io.projectroletemplatebinding\"},\"description\":\"ProjectRoleTemplateBinding is the object representing membership of a subject in a project with permissions\\nspecified by a given role template.\",\"pluralName\":\"management.cattle.io.projectroletemplatebindings\",\"resourceMethods\":[\"PUT\",\"PATCH\",\"GET\",\"DELETE\"],\"resourceFields\":null,\"collectionMethods\":[\"GET\",\"POST\"],\"attributes\":{\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"name\",\"description\":\"Name must be unique within a namespace. Is required when creating resources, although some resources may allow a client to request the generation of an appropriate name automatically. Name is primarily intended for creation idempotence and configuration definition. Cannot be updated. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names#names\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[0]\"},{\"name\":\"Age\",\"type\":\"date\",\"format\":\"\",\"description\":\"CreationTimestamp is a timestamp representing the server time when this object was created. It is not guaranteed to be set in happens-before order across separate operations. Clients may not set this value. It is represented in RFC3339 form and is in UTC.\\n\\nPopulated by the system. Read-only. Null for lists. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#metadata\",\"priority\":0,\"field\":\"$.metadata.fields[1]